Physical Exam: Cardiovascular: Normal peripheral pulses present bilaterally in the lower extremities. Neurological: Completely intact neurological examination of the lower extremities and perineum, with normal sensation and reflexes. No cardiovascular disease risk factors observed. Expected investigation results would include a normal serum morning total testosterone and a completely normal objective nocturnal penile tumescence test, demonstrating preserved physiological erectile capacity.
